n\n   630\t   they differ from what was saved (nothing is written for a bare run with\n   631\t   nothing saved), and answer the banner's lines about it.  A file that\n   632\t   cannot be written is a warning, never a refusal: the node still starts.\"\n   633\t  [dir saved resolved reset?]\n   634\t  (let [path (state/path dir)\n   635\t        changed (state/changed (or saved {}) resolved)]\n   636\t    (try\n   637\t      (cond\n   638\t        (and (nil? saved) (empty? resolved) (not reset?))\n   639\t        []\n   640\t\n   641\t        (nil? saved)\n   642\t        (do (state/save! dir resolved)\n   643\t            [(str \"state: \" (if reset? \"reset, \" \"\") \"saved to \" path\n   644\t                  \"; a bare yin-repl starts this node again\")])\n   645\t\n   646\t        (seq changed)\n   647\t        (do (state/save! dir resolved)\n   648\t            [(str \"state: resumed from \" path \" (\" (state/describe saved)\n   649\t                  \"); the command line changed \" (str/join \", \" changed)\n   650\t                  \"; saved\")])\n   651\t\n   652\t        :else\n   653\t        [(str \"state: resumed from \" path \" (\" (state/describe resolved) \")\")])\n   654\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   655\t                :clj Throwable\n   656\t                :cljs :default)\n   657\t             e\n   658\t        [(str \"state: WARNING: could not save \" path \": \"\n   659\t              (or (ex-message e) (str e)))]))))\n   660\t\n7:   in-memory `dao.jing` store, today's behaviour — `file:<dir>`, the\n8:   durable directory store (dao.space.store), or `dht:<dir>`, that store\n13:   scheme, an empty directory, a directory that cannot be opened, a host\n17:   The durable directory itself — the exclusive lock, HEAD, the validated\n37:   directory store of `file:<dir>` composed under a `dao.jing.dht` node\n43:  [\"mem\" (str file-scheme \"<dir>\") (str dht-scheme \"<dir>\")])\n47:  \"The `--index-store` value as a spec: `:mem`, or `{:type :file :dir dir}`\n48:   for `file:<dir>`.  A missing value, an unknown scheme, and an empty\n49:   directory are refused here — with the supported forms named — so the\n54:    (throw (ex-info \"--index-store needs a value: mem, file:<dir> or dht:<dir>\"\n61:    (let [dir (subs value (count file-scheme))]\n62:      (if (str/blank? dir)\n63:        (throw (ex-info \"--index-store file:<dir> needs a directory\"\n66:        {:type :file :dir dir}))\n69:    (let [dir (subs value (count dht-scheme))]\n70:      (if (str/blank? dir)\n71:        (throw (ex-info \"--index-store dht:<dir> needs a directory\"\n74:        {:type :dht :dir dir}))\n78:                         \"; supported: mem, file:<dir>, dht:<dir>\")\n88:  [{:keys [dir peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes manifest\n91:    (not (and (string? dir) (not (str/blank? dir))))\n92:    \"--index-store dht:<dir> needs a directory\"\n147:   map `{:type :file :dir dir}` with a non-empty directory string.  A DHT\n148:   store is `{:type :dht :dir dir}` plus its options, `dht-defaults`\n157:         (string? (:dir spec))\n158:         (not (str/blank? (:dir spec))))\n169:                         \"; supported: :mem, {:type :file :dir <dir>}, \"\n170:                         \"{:type :dht :dir <dir> ...}\")\n172:                     :supported [:mem {:type :file :dir \"<dir>\"}\n173:                                 {:type :dht :dir \"<dir>\"}]}))))\n178:   fresh in-memory `dao.jing` store; `{:type :file :dir dir}` is the\n179:   durable directory store at `dir` (dao.space.store/open): exclusive,\n180:   validating, its HEAD writer, recovery and lock on the handle.  A spec\n181:   this build cannot open is refused with its reason; a `dht:<dir>` spec\n188:      :file (durable/open (:dir checked))\n189:      :dht (throw (ex-info (str \"a dht:<dir> store is opened by \"\n195:  \"True when `store` is a durable directory store: its published index\n204:   content log and, in durable mode, the directory lock.  Idempotent.\"\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
