ed.** [main.cljc:688](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/yin-repl-state/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:688), [yin.repl.md:95](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/yin-repl-state/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:95). Two processes using `--name shared --index-store file:/tmp/a` and `--name shared --index-store file:/tmp/b` acquire different store locks but write the same `~/.yin/shared/state.edn`. Atomic replacement prevents partial files, not lost configuration updates. The documented exception is broader than in-memory nodes: it also includes durable stores whose directories differ from the state directory. Protect the state directory or document this limitation accurately.\n\n4. **P3 — Certain foreign configuration keys crash validation instead of producing a refusal. Confirmed on JVM.** [state.cljc:153](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/yin-repl-state/src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc:153). `{:version 1 :config {42 \"x\"}}` calls `name` on a number, throwing before the explicit validation branches. The resulting exception lacks the file/`--reset` diagnostic. Validate key types before converting them; add malformed-key coverage.\n\nThe normal merge precedence, whole replacement of repeated values, subcommand publishing removal, and empty `--reset` path are supported. Rendering avoids whitespace before closers, and host branches explicitly select ClojureDart. Persistence saves allowlisted flag values; `--dht-key` remains a path, and loaded key material does not enter the saved map. Write failures are caught as warnings, and synchronous startup refusals occur before saving.\n\nTest isolation looks sound: the three host entry points enable persistence, ordinary one-arity startup is stateless, persistence tests use scratch directories, and process tests supply `--no-state`. I did not edit files or rerun the verified checks.\n\n**Not ready to merge:** address the missing-value behavior and read-failure handling, and correct or enforce the shared-directory guarantee."}}
